From f055d04f18749a2156c1dfff997e86c6629419fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: colum <colum@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 10:54:08 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] server: TF_DS_ENERGY (off by default) puts a request's NVML
 energy in the done line, joules_total on rank 0's /metrics and a per-frame
 counter line on rank 1

The pair's energy use is unmeasured per request: `scripts/bench_overnight.py`'s Sampler polls power every 3 s (max only, no
integral, no attribution), and a reply's `tensorfold` block carries no energy field. NVML answers
`nvmlDeviceGetTotalEnergyConsumption` on both GB10s with rc 0 - a cumulative millijoule counter - so a request's energy is
an exact counter delta at its start and finish, with no sampling thread and no integration bias.

TF_DS_ENERGY (`1` or `on`; unset, `0`, `off` or anything else leave it off, as the series' switches do) reads that counter
on the request's own window. With it on, rank 0's `done` line ends with `energy_j=`, `idle_j=`, `round_from=` and
`round_to=`: the request's own delta, the counter's rise over an equal idle window before it (scaled from the gap between
the last finished request and this one's start; "-" when no such gap is at least as long as the request, so a gross
figure cannot attribute another request's draw), and the rank pair's wire frame ordinals. With the switch off nothing is
appended, so the line is byte for byte the base one and no driver call is made.

Rank 1 runs `tf-dsv41-lanes` (a follower: no HTTP server, no /metrics, no lane core and no `done` line), so its GPU's
figure cannot ride rank 0's line without the deferred rank-1-to-rank-0 exchange. The follower instead logs a new line
category of its own while the switch is on, one per frame it receives: `energy step=N mj=M`, the counter read before frame
N runs. Rank 1 checks every frame's step against its own counter (`error.OutOfStep`), so both ranks count the same
ordinals; `tools/energy.py` joins a request's `round_from`/`round_to` to those lines and takes the delta between the frame
at `round_from` and the frame after `round_to`, exactly. No existing parser matches the new line (`tools/zig/reuse_served.py`
reads `done` only); it is ~25 lines a second at one stream, and only while the switch is on.

`tensorfold:joules_total` (joules, a counter) joins `generation_tokens_total` on rank 0's /metrics, summing finished
requests' own windows; it is absent with the switch off, so the base body is unchanged. NVML's
`nvmlDeviceGetTotalEnergyConsumption` and `nvmlDeviceGetPowerUsage` are optional lookups of their own: a driver without
them still opens (the all-or-nothing symbol table of the CUDA runtime's libraries is the trap), and the figures degrade to
"-" rather than failing. The energy reader lives in `zig/src/core/energy.zig` (engine_api's `energy`), not a new CUDA
module: `zig/src/cuda/` has no NVML module in this tree, and the server, the engine seam and the follower all reach
engine_api. Replies and their bits are unchanged; the reply's `tensorfold` block is phase 2.

Tests: the switch parse ("1"/"on" on; unset, "0", "off", "" and anything else off), the off path (no counter read at all),
the window's arithmetic and both labels (gross delta, the equal idle window scaled from the gap, "-" when the gap is
shorter than the request), the absent driver and symbol path (the reader opens with no counter and every field is "-"),
and the suffix's exact text after the existing fields. `zig build test` and `zig/tests/server/zig_test.sh` pass. Not run on
a pair: the ordinals' alignment is the first live gate (docs/energy-per-request.md).
